496269d55099caa94f","event_uuid":"b1cc93a8-a2b3-429f-b639-c126cc24e81a","position":{"commit_sha":"0181e9a9151fe874ee254f9dee825ca52b0cb529","position":"1786498455463402772-b1cc93a8-a2b3-429f-b639-c126cc24e81a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-227_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"6f8df6b5-44f6-4ea4-b224-1eac4c95b0a7","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Triage (orphan sweep): RESOLVED. Landed as commit bf9fb62a6f5 ('d52a: thread Pass-1 usage into outputs+sidecar'). AC1: src/rebar/llm/plan_review/pass1.py:684 sets coverage['usage'] = aggregate_usage(call_records), surfaced on the batch step output at src/rebar/llm/plan_review/production_batch_runner.py:197 ('_usage': coverage.get('usage') or aggregate_usage([])). AC2: covered by tests/unit/workflow/test_pass1_usage.py — test_batch_runner_emits_usage_aggregate_with_prerequisites (:264) and test_attach_metrics_folds_token_totals_into_coverage_metrics (:307). Verified now: '.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/unit/workflow/test_pass1_usage.py -q' -> 15 passed.","timestamp":1786079828891954001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Closing verification (sanctioned non-force path), main @9bdb22f5887. Ticked all 3 ACs after independently re-verifying:\n\n- AC1: src/rebar/llm/plan_review/pass1.py sets coverage['usage'] = aggregate_usage(call_records) at the end of the finder run (the 'Per-call usage aggregation (story d52a)' block, ~line 684), and src/rebar/llm/plan_review/production_batch_runner.py:197 places it on the batch step output as '_usage': coverage.get('usage') or aggregate_usage([]). Pinned by tests/unit/workflow/test_pass1_usage.py::test_batch_runner_emits_usage_aggregate_with_prerequisites (line 264).\n- AC2: pinned by tests/unit/workflow/test_pass1_usage.py::test_attach_metrics_folds_token_totals_into_coverage_metrics (line 307).\n- AC3: verified now — '.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/unit/workflow/test_pass1_usage.py -q' -> 15 passed. 'make typecheck' -> Success: no issues found in 438 source files. 'make lint' is clean with the PINNED ruff ('uvx ruff@0.16.1 check src tests' -> All checks passed; format --check -> 1721 files already formatted); note this checkout's .venv carries a stale ruff 0.15.19 against pyproject's pinned ruff==0.16.1, which reports 101 spurious BLE001/T201 errors. For the Gerrit half: commit bf9fb62a6f ('d52a: thread Pass-1 usage into outputs+sidecar') is confirmed an ancestor of origin/main ('git merge-base --is-ancestor bf9fb62a6f origin/main' succeeds), and main only accepts changes submitted through Gerrit carrying both LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 — so the landing requirement is met by construction.\n\nCaveat recorded honestly: a full 'pytest -m \"not integration and not external\"' run here is 10821 passed / 18 failed, but none of the failures touch this change. 17 are artifacts of this venv or a concurrent agent (missing 'ddgs' optional dep, stale botocore 1.40.61 < 1.43.64, the stale ruff above, and a criteria-vocabulary scan reaching into .claude/worktrees/); one is a genuine unrelated pre-existing failure, tests/unit/test_path_injection_guards.py::test_rerun_502_body_has_no_exception_detail.","timestamp":1786086626505748001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"CORRECTION — I have UN-ticked all three ACs I ticked in my previous comment. This ticket is NOT resolved, and the earlier orphan-sweep triage (and my own first pass) was wrong.\n\n'rebar review-plan 514d-a8d8-bb3a-482d' (no --force) returned BLOCK, and its G1G2 finding is CORRECT and I confirmed it independently:\n\nThis ticket's title and Context target the REVIEW BOT's CloudWatch token totals — the follow-up to fd71/clayish-basaltine-bug, whose counts come from _attach_code_review_metrics. What actually landed in bf9fb62a6f ('d52a: thread Pass-1 usage into outputs+sidecar') covers only the PLAN-REVIEW path:\n- src/rebar/llm/plan_review/pass1.py sets coverage['usage'], and src/rebar/llm/plan_review/production_batch_runner.py:197 emits outputs['_usage'] — plan-review's ProductionBatchRunner only.\n- The finalize unit test cited as AC2 evidence, tests/unit/workflow/test_pass1_usage.py::test_attach_metrics_folds_token_totals_into_coverage_metrics (line 313), calls _attach_plan_review_metrics — the plan-review assembler, not the code-review one.\n- The CODE-REVIEW finder batch runner, src/rebar/llm/code_review/batch_runner.py, contains ZERO occurrences of 'usage' — 'grep -n usage src/rebar/llm/code_review/batch_runner.py' returns nothing.\n- src/rebar/llm/code_review/finalize.py:139-141 still documents the gap in the present tense: 'Today that is the Pass-2 verify + Pass-3 decide agent steps — the Pass-1 finder batch does not surface _usage on its step output (follow-up)'.\n\nSo the undercount this ticket exists to fix is still live on the review-bot/CloudWatch path. Remaining work: mirror the plan-review aggregation into code_review/batch_runner.py so its batch step output carries _usage, and extend _attach_code_review_metrics (and delete the stale comment at finalize.py:139-141) with a code-review finalize unit test.\n\nLeaving this ticket OPEN. No --force / --force-close was used.","timestamp":1786087071869748001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implementation pushed as Gerrit change 1600 (worktree ../514d-cr-usage, commit ec6a014b19).\n\nDESIGN NOTE on AC2 ('same helper and shape as d52a'). The plan review PASSed but raised a correct advisory I verified independently: aggregate_usage() (plan_review/pass1.py) returns a NESTED payload {per_call, per_criterion, totals}, while finalize._attach_code_review_metrics folds _usage FLAT — it reads input_tokens/output_tokens/cache_read_tokens/cache_write_tokens at the TOP level of the dict (finalize.py:169-172). So a literal shape-mirror (emitting the nested aggregate as _usage) would have folded to ZERO and left the CloudWatch under-report exactly as it was. The divergence is in the two CONSUMERS: plan-review's _attach_plan_review_metrics folds the nested form; code-review's finalize folds the flat form.\n\nResolution, which honors AC2's INTENT (one helper, no second convention) while actually fixing the undercount:\n- same helper: CodeReviewBatchRunner builds one per-call record per overlay dispatch via sizing.usage_record and aggregates with aggregate_usage.\n- same payload, same place: the full nested aggregate rides on batch_plan['usage'] — the same slot plan-review uses (coverage['usage']) — so raw per-call attribution stays reconstructable.\n- the step-output _usage is that aggregate's ['totals'] (flat), i.e. what this path's consumer actually reads.\nAttribution here is whole, not split: each dispatch is a single agent call covering exactly one criterion, so plan-review's equal-split approximation never applies.\n\nRED verified before GREEN: with the emit change reverted and the new tests in place, test_finder_batch_tokens_reach_the_finalized_totals fails 'assert 1 == 131' — only the verify step's tokens counted, which IS the reported bug. After the change: 131/26/5/7, total 157.\n\nGates run in the worktree: make lint clean; make typecheck -> Success, 498 source files; pytest tests/unit -k 'code_review or batch or usage' -> 614 passed, 3 skipped. finalize.py's folding arithmetic is untouched (only its stale gap comment replaced) and the pre-existing finalize token tests in tests/unit/test_review_bot_token_metrics.py pass unmodified.\n\nNote: the new test module was created at the path recorded in file_impact, tests/unit/test_code_review_finalize.py (that file did not previously exist).","timestamp":1786498049163802001}],"created_at":1784855908433883001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"31c3103b-0021-46f5-8060-192f1a95e9cd","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"fd71-a0a0-d9b0-4769"},{"link_uuid":"b1cc93a8-a2b3-429f-b639-c126cc24e81a","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"8dc9-daa5-125c-406f"}],"description":"## Context\n\nThe review bot's reported token totals are incomplete: the Pass-1 finder batch does not surface its\nusage on the batch step output, so the finalize step has nothing to fold in and the CloudWatch\ntotals under-report every code review by the whole Pass-1 finder leg.\n\n**This ticket is now scoped to the CODE-REVIEW half only.** The plan-review half of the original\nscope already landed under ticket `d52a`: `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/pass1.py:684` sets\n`coverage[\"usage\"] = aggregate_usage(call_records)`, and\n`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/production_batch_runner.py:199` surfaces it as\n`\"_usage\": coverage.get(\"usage\") or aggregate_usage([])`. Re-scoped 2026-08-09 after a status\naudit found that half delivered and this half untouched; do not re-do the plan-review work.\n\nWhat remains, verified outstanding on `origin/main`:\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/code_review/batch_runner.py:130` emits `outputs={\"findings\", \"criteria_count\",\n  \"batch_plan\"}` — there is no `usage` key anywhere in the file.\n- `src/rebar/llm/code_review/finalize.py:139-141` carries a present-tense comment recording the gap\n  (\"the Pass-1 finder batch does not surface `_usage` on its step output (follow-up)\"), which is\n  now this ticket and becomes stale the moment it is fixed.\n- `src/rebar/llm/code_review/finalize.py:169-172` ALREADY folds `_usage` into the totals when a step\n  emits it, so the consuming side needs no change — this is an emit-side fix.\n\n## Plan\n\nMirror the shape `d52a` established on the plan-review side rather than inventing a second\nconvention: aggregate the Pass-1 finder call records in the code-review batch runner and emit them\nunder the same `_usage` step-output key `finalize.py` already reads. Then delete the stale\nfollow-up comment in `finalize.py`, because a comment describing a closed gap is worse than none.\n\nKeep the change emit-side only. Do not modify `finalize.py`'s folding arithmetic — it is already\ncorrect and covered; touching it would widen the blast radius for no gain.\n\n## Testing\n\nA code-review finalize unit test that asserts the finder-batch usage reaches the folded totals: it\nmust FAIL before the emit change (the key is absent, so the fold contributes zero) and pass after.\nAssert on the folded total rather than on the presence of the key, so the test proves the number is\nactually complete rather than that a dict has a key.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `src/rebar/llm/code_review/batch_runner.py` emits Pass-1 finder token usage on its batch step\n      output under the same `_usage` key that `finalize.py:169-172` already consumes.\n- [ ] The aggregation uses the same helper and shape as the plan-review side established by `d52a`,\n      so the two paths do not diverge into two conventions.\n- [ ] The stale gap comment at `src/rebar/llm/code_review/finalize.py:139-141` is removed.\n- [ ] A held-out unit test asserts the finder-batch usage is included in the finalized code-review\n      totals, verified RED before the emit change and GREEN after.\n- [ ] `finalize.py`'s existing folding arithmetic is unchanged, and the existing code-review\n      finalize tests pass unmodified.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/code_review/batch_runner.py","reason":"emit Pass-1 finder usage on the batch step output under the _usage key"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/code_review/finalize.py","reason":"remove the now-stale follow-up gap comment; folding arithmetic unchanged"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_code_review_finalize.py","reason":"held-out test that finder usage reaches the folded totals"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","8dc9-daa5-125c-406f"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"6b99a4f1-3081-458b-9316-22d2fb368ed2","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"514d-a8d8-bb3a-482d","ticket_type":"task","title":"code-review: surface Pass-1 finder token usage on the batch step output","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["bc890abf-31e0-4fc6-919a-b9efcd8360b7","31c3103b-0021-46f5-8060-192f1a95e9cd","ff3b28f5-c32e-464f-90de-73db1b741427","d32dc1e7-5146-4d9b-bdb8-22b53513d5fa","7a568939-cffb-4b43-b2be-17fed82d984c","12a755d0-5e2a-4e06-a2ed-fa01061de31f","c7a65b67-fb2d-4d05-b565-96490b1115ba","8e191473-f257-4ba6-bb90-2aae2e18772d","87972b54-b505-4ea4-bc4c-2e7ed90c9054","6e792d7d-6cd1-4c54-ab5a-72634c51aa53","2f81a858-cdf1-4115-88ef-ebb9ae36e517","6b99a4f1-3081-458b-9316-22d2fb368ed2","27d0ad1f-42f0-4c90-b017-eab35292d7db","7693b9b0-e18b-4f90-9c16-c75ff3f89538","b1cc93a8-a2b3-429f-b639-c126cc24e81a"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786498455463402773,"uuid":"0e33f3cf-eed3-4abe-afc5-8695d03b17b8"}